ID: B3-Ch04b-Beg4
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_aura_hardening >= 3 || v_premonition >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_premonition < 3)
#if(v_premonition >= 3) {
 

"Alright, Billy Bob," I say. "I'm coming over."

I step past the edge of the rack, my boots clicking on the flagstones. Billy Bob stays pressed against the table, trembling, his hands tucked out of sight behind his back.

A violent flash seizes my mind—a plume of white-hot flame erupting from the flagstone ahead, scorching skin to ash in a fraction of a heartbeat.

I throw myself backward.

The air cracks. A jet of pressurized flame roars up from the seam in the floor right where my next stride would have landed, licking the ceiling tiles before venting out.

A concealed burner mechanism beneath the stone. The hands tucked behind his back were working a toggle on the underside of the tabletop.

As the flare dies down, Billy Bob lunges through the smoke, a serrated knife raised in his right fist. Before he covers three paces, Kate fires four icicles straight through his neck and chest. He crashes face-first across the scorched flagstone and lies still.

"I should have known," Kate mutters, lowering her hands. "He gave up the cipher too fast."

}
#if(v_aura_hardening >= 3 && v_premonition < 3) {
 

"Alright, Billy Bob," I say. "I'm coming over."

I step past the edge of the rack, my boots clicking on the flagstones. Billy Bob stays pressed against the table, trembling, his hands tucked out of sight behind his back.

The moment my boot presses the center tile, a jet of pressurized flame roars up from the floor, engulfing me in a blinding pillar of fire. My hardened aura locks tight against the heat, deflecting the lethal wash, though the searing wave still forces me to stumble backward out of the column.

A concealed burner mechanism beneath the stone. The hands tucked behind his back were working a toggle on the underside of the tabletop.

As the flare dies down, Billy Bob lunges through the smoke, a serrated knife raised in his right fist. Before he covers three paces, Kate fires four icicles straight through his neck and chest. He crashes face-first across the scorched flagstone and lies still.

"I should have known," Kate mutters, lowering her hands. "He gave up the cipher too fast."

}
