"Alright, Billy Bob," I say. "I'm coming over."

I step past the edge of the rack, my boots clicking on the flagstones. Billy Bob stays pressed against the table, trembling, his hands tucked out of sight behind his back.

The moment my boot presses the center tile, a jet of pressurized flame roars up from the floor, engulfing me in a blinding pillar of fire. The agony hits instantly, searing skin and lungs before I can even recoil, and the world goes black before my body hits the stone.

}
