ID: B3-Ch04b-Billy5
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_aura_hardening >= 3 || v_premonition >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_premonition < 3)
#if(v_premonition >= 3) {
 

"Kate, wait," I say. "Don't kill him yet."

"Why not?" Kate asks.

Instead of answering, I slide my dagger from its sheath and advance toward the bench, reversing my grip to lead with the pommel. Billy Bob recoils, his hips hitting the metal frame. With nowhere left to retreat, he presses against the table, trembling, his hands tucked out of sight behind his back.

A violent premonition hits my mind—flames tearing up through the stone directly under my feet, charring bone in an instant.

Instead of jumping back, I pivot and lunge forward in a low sprint, crossing the danger zone before the toggle can cycle. The burner vents a split-second too late behind my heels, and I close the distance in a breath.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening >= 3 && v_premonition < 3) {
 

"Kate, wait," I say. "Don't kill him yet."

"Why not?" Kate asks.

Instead of answering, I slide my dagger from its sheath and advance toward the bench, reversing my grip to lead with the pommel. Billy Bob recoils, his hips hitting the metal frame. With nowhere left to retreat, he presses against the table, trembling, his hands tucked out of sight behind his back.

The flagstone under my foot sinks an inch, and a pillar of fire erupts around my shins. My hardened aura takes the brunt of the heat, and without breaking stride, I power through the wall of flame and close the distance in a breath.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening < 3 && v_premonition < 3) {
 

"Kate, wait," I say. "Don't kill him yet."

"Why not?" Kate asks.

Instead of answering, I slide my dagger from its sheath and advance toward the bench, reversing my grip to lead with the pommel. Billy Bob recoils, his hips hitting the metal frame. With nowhere left to retreat, he presses against the table, trembling, his hands tucked out of sight behind his back.

The flagstone under my foot sinks an inch, and a pillar of fire erupts around my shins. The searing heat engulfs me before I can leap away, tearing through flesh and bone until consciousness snaps.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening >= 3 || v_premonition >= 3) {
 Billy Bob's hands whip around from behind his back with a concealed blade, but I swing the heavy pommel of my dagger into his temple before he can raise the point. His eyes roll back, and he folds across the floor in a dead heap.

I glance down at the scorched seam near the table leg. The hands behind his back were reaching for a sub-table trap trigger.

Kate steps up beside the unconscious lessathi, looking down with a frown. "Why leave him breathing? The moment he wakes, he'll return to draining mages in the dungeon."

}
