 "Sure. Why not?" I say, as I take the crossbow out of my backpack and shoot Billy Bob in the head, killing him instantly.

"The Overseer protocol expresses gratitude," the machine says.

"Right," I say. "Now how many guards know we're here? Are we fighting our way down, or can we pull a clean extraction?"

"Biliborrathrathsarran initiated an alarm routine upon your entry, but I suspended the transmission to facilitate our discussion," the Overseer says. "No units are currently routed to this room. I will reactivate the broadcast following your departure so security may retrieve the remains."

"Then we're done here," Melindra says. "Breynan, call transit."

"Calling now," Breynan says.

He pulls his transceiver from his coat, keys the crystal, and speaks into the grille. "Barry! Can you read me?"

"Breynan?" the operator's voice crackles back. "Where have you been? I've been hailing your unit for twenty minutes! Never mind—we have squads queuing in the corridor. Stand by for extraction!"

"Do it now!" Breynan says.

"Locking coordinates," the operator says. White light floods the workshop, vibrating deep in our bones as the teleportation field takes hold.

"Farewell," the Overseer intones as the room dissolves around us. "Our next meeting will occur shortly."

}
