ID: B3-Ch04b-Stuck
TEXT:

 "Hey, Overseer! That all you've got?" I shout into the vaulted ceiling. "Send the rest of the scrap!"

Silence. Only the distant echo of garrison klaxons.

"Let me try transit again," Breynan says, catching his breath. "The garrison is held up behind the blade corridor—they won't clear that trap quickly. We have time to pull a clean extraction."

He pulls his transceiver, keys the crystal, and speaks into the grille.

"Barry, are you there?"
  	
"I'm here!" the operator's voice crackles through clearly. "Where did you drop the signal? Never mind—we have forty agents queuing in the transit hall and I need the platform clear. Stand by for extraction!"

"Do it now," Breynan says.

"Locking coordinates," the operator says. White light floods the gallery, vibrating deep in our bones.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch04b-Ending, v_current_scene = B3-Ch04b-Ending)


ID: B3-Ch04b-Ending
TEXT:

 The white glare snaps away, leaving us standing on the raised transit platform inside the rebel caverns. Barry the teleporter operator sits hunched over his brass switchboard, shouting over a dense crowd of armed rebels and civilian families crowding the chamber.

"Clear the platform!" he barks without looking up. "Move into the primary tunnels! We have three more extraction waves incoming!"

"What happened while we were on the surface?" Breynan asks, stepping off the dais.

"You mean you haven't heard?" Barry the operator looks up, eyes wide. "Where have you people been?"

"Underground, Barry," Breynan says dryly. "What happened?"

"Complete lockdown," the operator says, throwing a bank of levers as another flash illuminates the far corner. "The city gates are sealed, patrols are sweeping every quarter, and citizens are being dragged out of their homes. Undriel put the entire capital under martial law."

"Why?" Breynan asks, brow furrowing. "What triggered it?"

"The king issued a proclamation an hour ago," the operator says, hands flying across his dials. "His brother was assassinated in Thilias, and the killers are hiding inside Ollendor. The garrison has orders to search every building from the sewers to the eaves."

"The king's brother was killed in Thilias?" I ask, keeping my tone carefully neutral. "How did word reach Ollendor so fast?"

"Who else?" the operator says, wiping sweat from his forehead. "The ambassador from Thilias has returned."

choice("Next chapter", B3-Ch05a-Intro, v_next_chapter_crash = 1, v_current_scene = B3-Ch05a-Intro, v_chapter_save_counter = 5, v_checkpoint_rich = 1, special:checkpoint_save)


